      "encoded": 5376,
      "evidence": "tools/native-abi/probe.generated.c compiled against this version's canonical headers; every bound prototype, struct size, alignment, field offset and field size in this manifest verified by the C compiler, and every by-value aggregate verified at run time through tools/native-abi/valueprobe.generated.c."
    }
  ],
  "by_value_aggregate_rule": {
    "admitted_classification": "INTEGER",
    "max_size_bytes": 16,
    "rule": "A by-value aggregate parameter is bound only when the System V AMD64 ABI classifies every one of its eightbytes as INTEGER and its size is at most 16 bytes. Such a parameter is passed as one scalar argument per eightbyte, which occupies exactly the argument registers or stack slots the aggregate itself would occupy. An aggregate with any floating-point eightbyte (SSE class) or larger than 16 bytes is refused by the generator and the route that needs it is left unbound and reported as blocked.",
    "why": "CFFI cannot pass a structure by value without cffi-libffi, and cffi-libffi requires libffi headers and a C compiler at load time, which a released CNA-Lisp must not. See docs/native-abi.md."
  },
